DESCRIPTION >
    - `stars_count.pipe` provides "new stars" (period-specific, non-cumulative) analytics for a
    project or curated collection, replacing `activities_count.pipe` for stars only.
    - Built directly on top of `stars_cumulative_count.pipe`: in granularity mode, a period's "new
    stars" is just that bucket's cumulative total minus the previous bucket's - correct regardless
    of whether the underlying number came from a GitHub snapshot or a GitLab per-event count, so
    there's no separate GitHub/GitLab branching in the bucketed mode at all.
    - **Can go negative for a bucket** - GitHub's snapshot total is the platform's current net
    count (stars minus unstars), so a bucket where unstars outpaced new stars nets negative. Real,
    not a bug. GitLab's own contribution to the same bucket can't go negative (it's an event
    tally), but the combined number can.
    - **Backfill-inflation caveat (same as the already-reworked sibling star pipes)**: the very
    first bucket where a repo's snapshot history exists shows that repo's *entire* historical
    total as "new", since there's no earlier snapshot to diff against. Repos whose star-snapshot
    backfill hasn't reached back to the start of the requested range will show an inflated
    first-seen bucket.
    - Exactly one of `project` / `collectionSlug` must be given, same contract as
    `stars_cumulative_count.pipe` / `activities_filtered.pipe`. `bucketId` is required alongside
    `collectionSlug` for the same reason `stars_cumulative_count.pipe` needs it - both collection
    branches here return no rows unless it's defined. The insights backend's Tinybird client
    already resolves and injects `bucketId` transparently for both `project` and `collectionSlug`
    on every pipe call, same as it does for every other pipe today.
    - Parameters: `project`, `collectionSlug`, `bucketId`, `repos`, `startDate`, `endDate`,
    `granularity` - identical to `stars_cumulative_count.pipe`, passed straight through.
    - Response:
    - Without granularity: `activityCount` (single row)
    - With granularity: `startDate`, `endDate`, `activityCount` per bucket
    - Response field names deliberately match `activities_count.pipe` so `stars.ts` can swap the
    pipe name with no other code changes.

TOKEN "insights-app-token" READ

NODE stars_count_repo_scope
DESCRIPTION >
    Same GitHub repo scoping as `stars_cumulative_count.pipe`'s `stars_repo_scope` node,
    duplicated here since Tinybird nodes only see their own pipe file.

SQL >
    %
    {% if defined(collectionSlug) %}
        SELECT r.id AS repositoryId
        FROM repositories r FINAL
        WHERE
            {% if defined(bucketId) %}
                isNull (r.deletedAt)
                AND r.enabled = true
                AND r.excluded = false
                AND r.url LIKE 'https://github.com/%'
                AND r.segmentId IN (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered_by_collection)
                {% if defined(repos) %}
                    AND has(
                        arrayMap(
                            x -> lower(x),
                            {{ Array(repos, 'String', description="Repository URLs", required=False) }}
                        ),
                        lower(r.url)
                    )
                {% end %}
            {% else %} 1 = 0
            {% end %}
    {% else %}
        SELECT r.id AS repositoryId
        FROM repositories r FINAL
        INNER JOIN insightsProjects i FINAL ON r.insightsProjectId = i.id
        WHERE
            isNull (r.deletedAt)
            AND r.enabled = true
            AND r.excluded = false
            AND r.url LIKE 'https://github.com/%'
            AND isNull (i.deletedAt)
            AND i.enabled = 1
            AND r.segmentId = (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered)
            {% if defined(repos) %}
                AND has(
                    arrayMap(
                        x -> lower(x),
                        {{ Array(repos, 'String', description="Repository URLs", required=False) }}
                    ),
                    lower(r.url)
                )
            {% end %}
    {% end %}

NODE stars_count_bucketed
DESCRIPTION >
    Granularity mode: diffs consecutive buckets of `stars_cumulative_count`'s running total - "new
    stars" in a bucket is just that bucket's cumulative total minus the previous bucket's. First
    bucket in range diffs against 0 (see backfill-inflation caveat above).

SQL >
    %
    {% if defined(granularity) %}
        SELECT
            startDate,
            endDate,
            toInt64(cumulativeActivityCount) - toInt64(
                coalesce(lagInFrame(cumulativeActivityCount) OVER (ORDER BY startDate ASC), 0)
            ) AS activityCount
        FROM stars_cumulative_count
        ORDER BY startDate ASC
    {% else %} SELECT toDate(now()) AS startDate, toDate(now()) AS endDate, 0 AS activityCount
    {% end %}

NODE stars_count_summary
DESCRIPTION >
    No-granularity mode: total "new stars" across (startDate, endDate] - a star captured/counted
    exactly at startDate belongs to the prior period's baseline, not this one. GitHub = total as
    of endDate minus total as of startDate (0 if a repo has no snapshot yet at startDate - same
    backfill-inflation caveat as the bucketed mode, can also go negative on net unstars). GitLab =
    plain per-event range count, `platform != 'github'`.

SQL >
    %
    {% if not defined(granularity) %}
        WITH
            github_at_end AS (
                SELECT sum(starCount) AS total
                FROM
                    (
                        SELECT argMax(starCount, (capturedAt, updatedAt)) AS starCount
                        FROM repositoryStarSnapshots
                        WHERE
                            repositoryId IN (SELECT repositoryId FROM stars_count_repo_scope)
                            {% if defined(endDate) %}
                                AND capturedAt
                                <= {{ DateTime(endDate, description="Range end", required=False) }}
                            {% end %}
                        GROUP BY repositoryId
                    )
            ),
            github_at_start AS (
                SELECT sum(starCount) AS total
                FROM
                    (
                        SELECT argMax(starCount, (capturedAt, updatedAt)) AS starCount
                        FROM repositoryStarSnapshots
                        WHERE
                            repositoryId IN (SELECT repositoryId FROM stars_count_repo_scope)
                            {% if defined(startDate) %}
                                AND capturedAt
                                <= {{ DateTime(startDate, description="Range start", required=False) }}
                            {% else %} AND 1 = 0
                            {% end %}
                        GROUP BY repositoryId
                    )
            ),
            gitlab_new AS (
                SELECT count() AS c
                FROM
                    {% if defined(collectionSlug) %} activityRelations_collection_bucket_routing
                    {% else %} activityRelations_bucket_routing
                    {% end %} as a
                WHERE
                    {% if defined(collectionSlug) %}
                        {% if defined(bucketId) %}
                            segmentId IN (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered_by_collection)
                            AND a.collectionSlug = {{ String(collectionSlug) }}
                        {% else %} 1 = 0
                        {% end %}
                    {% else %} segmentId = (SELECT segmentId FROM segments_filtered)
                    {% end %}
                    AND type = 'star'
                    AND platform != 'github'
                    AND channel NOT IN (SELECT channel FROM repos_to_channels_excluded)
                    {% if defined(repos) %}
                        AND channel IN (SELECT channel FROM repos_to_channels)
                    {% end %}
                    {% if defined(startDate) %}
                        AND timestamp
                        > {{ DateTime(startDate, description="Range start", required=False) }}
                    {% end %}
                    {% if defined(endDate) %}
                        AND timestamp
                        <= {{ DateTime(endDate, description="Range end", required=False) }}
                    {% end %}
            )
        SELECT
            toInt64(coalesce((SELECT total FROM github_at_end), 0))
            - toInt64(coalesce((SELECT total FROM github_at_start), 0))
            + (SELECT c FROM gitlab_new) AS activityCount
    {% else %} SELECT 0 AS activityCount
    {% end %}

NODE stars_count_final
SQL >
    %
    {% if defined(granularity) %} SELECT startDate, endDate, activityCount FROM stars_count_bucketed
    {% else %} SELECT activityCount FROM stars_count_summary
    {% end %}
